+// The application locale this launch presents, or empty when the host's own is
+// to be inherited.
+//
+// Precedence, and it is the launch contract's rather than a new one:
+//
+//   `--fingerprint-locale`, which is where an operator's own choice and the
+//   launchers' prelaunch GeoIP answer both arrive;
+//
+//   the installed profile's own `locale.accept_languages`, which is what an
+//   authored `--apostate-profile` carries and what composition writes;
+//
+//   kComposedDefaultLocale, because absence of a resolved locale has to mean a
+//   defined value or the served locale becomes a property of the operator's
+//   shell.
+//
+// Empty means inherit, and exactly three launches get it: `--fingerprint=host`
+// and its off spellings, which install no profile because the host is the
+// thing being presented; a launch the compiled catalogue cannot serve, which
+// inherits the host on every axis, so pinning the locale alone would leave one
+// composed surface on an otherwise host-owned launch; and any process of a
+// browser that is not ours, where `--apostate-profile` is simply absent.
+//
+// Read off the command line, never through `Profile::Get()`, and the
+// difference is load-bearing: `Get()` caches its answer on first call and that
+// call can precede the hook that installs the profile, which is the defect
+// patch 0110 was bitten by. The command line is final from
+// `InstallComposedProfile` onwards and is the one channel a child also has, so
+// browser and child answer identically without either consulting the other.
+BASE_EXPORT std::string ComposedApplicationLocale();
